<title>USA: Baltimore Gas to call $16.1 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Baltimore Gas to call $16.1 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Baltimore Gas and Electric Co announced Monday a partial call of $16.1 million principal amount of its 7-1/8 percent series first refunding mortgage bonds in connection with the company's annual sinking fund.</p>
<p>The redemption of the bonds, which are due January 1, 2002, would be made by Bankers Trust Co, it said.</p>
<p>Bonds called for the sinking fund would be redeemed in whole or in part on August 28 at 100 percent of principal, plus accrued interest.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
